Z||000000||86seyellow||08-10-2001||02:25 PM||||well got the car back today. Mechanic verified no 3 cylinder isnt firing good and has real low compression. so my question is, can I drive this vehicel or is this thing going to sieze on me?? hwo do I redo the thing. Mecahnic thinks it is probably the valve. ANy ideas, PLEASE HELP<BR><P>------------------<BR>if you saw a yellow streak go by you really fast it was a fiero<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TONY_C||08-10-2001||03:08 PM||||Well, the way to tell if the valve is bad or not is to add a squirt or two of oil into the cylinder by removing the spark plug and checking the compression again.  if the compression goes up, the valve is ok and the problem is most likely piston rings.  Assuming the compression doesnt get better with oil, the way to proceed is with a complete valve job.  another rpossibility, although remote is that you have a collapsed intake valve lifter on the #3 cylinder which is not allowing air/fuel into the cylinder. from my experience though, it sounds like your mechanic did the oil test since he states he thinks it's a valve and i wpould tend to agree with him.  Assuming the bottom end of the engine is in good shape, i.e. not too high mileage, this should be the best thing to do. aside from the obvious loss of power, a leaky valve will not cause further engine damage.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||08-10-2001||03:56 PM||||My understanding is that if squirting oil in the cylinder makes the compression go up then it is the rings not the valves that need repair.  <P>The oil fills the space between the ring groove and the ring and between the ring and the cylinder wall and consequently gives higher cylinder pressures.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bill 88||08-11-2001||11:26 AM||||That is what was said Carrolles.  But I had to read it twice to get it too.  I agree with the diagnosis.  But one other thing it could be is a broken spring, but that would make lots of noise.  I know, I had one on one of my other vehicles. (I can't say the name, but it starts with F.)||||reg||1
